WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:06.359
You would think that with the rapid industrialisation
of our world in the past 100 years that there

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:08.549
would be nowhere left to hide.

00:00:08.549 --> 00:00:14.980
Well, the Stone Age civilization of the Sentinelese
people have managed to say bugger off to cheeseburgers

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:20.490
and smartphones and permanently isolate themselves
from the rest of the world.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.369
The Sentinelese haven’t had a single pork
scratching of contact with other humans, and

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:31.429
the few bump-ins they have had, have all ended
up with the intruders becoming pork scratchings.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:37.250
There are estimated to be around 100 so-called
“uncontacted” tribes left in the world,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.370
people who have had little-to-no outside contact.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:46.519
One such tribe lives on the remote North Sentinel
island in the Bay of Bengal, between India

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:47.990
and Malaysia.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:53.980
There are estimated to be anywhere between
50-500 members of the tribe, and that incredibly

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:59.330
varied number is just a sentiment to how little
we’ve been able to find out about them.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:05.010
But what we do know about these genital-waggling
tribespeople, after observing them from boats

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:09.560
and helicopters, is that they are incomprehensibly
primitive.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:16.700
They use stone-age tools, and live a hunter-gatherer
lifestyle and have no understanding of agriculture

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:22.020
and amazingly, they haven’t even discovered
how to make fire.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.330
They simply wait for lightning to strike and
they then attempt to keep the embers burning

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.490
for as long as possible, seriously.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:33.030
I imagine it’s really annoying when you
planned to cook a Sunday roast but you can’t

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.390
because there hasn’t been any lightning
that week.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:40.420
It’s thought that the Sentinelese people
are directly descended from the very first

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:47.200
human populations to emerge from Africa and
to this day their methods of hunting and living

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.479
have remained fairly unchanged, for over 60,000
years.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:57.270
They have remained uncontacted for now, but
not for our lack of trying.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.890
There have been numerous documented attempts
to make contact with the tribe and all of

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:07.020
them have ended with the visitors being shooed
away with a hail of arrows or they have been

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.720
captured by the tribespeople and brutally
murdered.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.460
Two fishermen were illegally fishing in the
waters surrounding North Sentinel island.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:20.540
The men got so drunk that they were unable
to sail back to the mainland and instead fell

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:26.950
asleep aboard their boat, which during the
night drifted onto the shore of North Sentinel

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.200
island.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.610
The tribe ran out of the jungle and attacked
the two men with arrows and spears, leaving

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.810
them for dead.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:38.590
A few days later the Indian coastguard sent
a helicopter to recover the men’s bodies

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.670
from the island, which were viewable from
the air, but as the helicopter neared the

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:49.040
island it was met with a rain of arrows from
the ground, so the helicopter ran away with

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.760
its tail between its legs.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:58.110
They don’t even contact other local tribes,
most tribes in the area share a similar language

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:04.989
but the Sentilenese have their own, very unique
language that no-one else can interpret.

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:10.050
But you can’t really blame them for their
hostility towards outsiders, their only previous

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:16.050
contact with other humans ended up with two
of their fellow tribespeople dying.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:21.660
During the British Empire, those well-dressed
tea enthusiasts, oh wait that’s me, thought

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.380
the entire world was theirs for the taking,
and they would go to extreme lengths to do

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:27.380
so.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:32.340
They had a system for entrapping isolated
tribes and taking their land.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.620
First they would kidnap a few tribe members
and take them back to the British camp, where

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:42.090
they would treat them like royalty and shower
them with gifts then return them to their

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.090
people.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:48.030
In the hope that the rest of the tribe would
go “oh okay, these British guys aren’t

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:53.819
too bad”, enabling the British to sweep
in and take their land without hostility.

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:58.870
The plucky Brits were pros at this and they
succeeded time and time again, until they

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.430
tried it with the Sentilenese people.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:06.060
The British sailed to North Sentinel island,
which is believed to be the first outsider

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:12.430
contact with the island and they kidnapped
two elderly tribespeople and four young children,

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:17.160
they took them back to the nearby British
settlement at Port Blair and began their friendly

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.650
indoctrination of the captured tribespeople.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:26.939
A few days later the two elderly members got
sick and died, so the British thought “we’re

00:04:26.939 --> 00:04:30.740
probably not going to do too well at winning
over the trust of the rest of the Sentinelese

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.169
people after we just killed their granny and
grandpops”.

00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:39.120
So they let the children go and simply left
the island alone.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.839
It wasn’t understood why the two elderly
tribespeople died at the time but we now know

00:04:44.839 --> 00:04:50.259
from encounters with other tribes, that the
years of isolation has left their immune systems

00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:56.159
several thousand years behind the developed
world, so diseases which modern medicine has

00:04:56.159 --> 00:05:02.900
long since conquered such as influenza and
smallpox can easily devastate an entire uncontacted

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:07.120
tribe after just a single encounter with an
outsider.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.999
The Indian government has since realised that
the Sentinelese are rather annoyed at our

00:05:10.999 --> 00:05:15.949
incessant attempts to be their friends and
have recently passed a law which banned all

00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:20.099
contact with the tribe, thinking they are
best left alone.

00:05:20.099 --> 00:05:24.639
A jail sentence awaits anyone who attempts
to travel to the island.

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:30.550
The last we saw of the tribe was when the
Indian Ocean tsunami hit the area in 2004,

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:35.169
killing more than 230,000 people in 24 countries.

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:39.589
The Indian Navy flew a helicopter over North
Sentinel island just to make sure they had

00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:45.339
survived the deadly tsunami, fearing the entire
tribe could have been killed.

00:05:45.339 --> 00:05:50.830
But as they neared the island the helicopter
was once again hit with arrows, indicating

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:56.270
that the Sentinelese people were alive and
well and thankfully up to their same old violent

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:16.069
tricks.

